-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       3D Stock Car Championship
  Publisher   Ace Software, 1988
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        3D Stock Car Championship (1988)(Firebird Software).z80
  MD5         56f151581bbcada775bb9e180bf4df9d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Backgrounds
              needs a 2MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Backgrounds (needs a 2MB Next),
              chosen on the menu, off by default.
  Enhanced    Backgrounds: a painted picture for each of the 25 circuits and
              for the menu, 320 x 256. The game's own stands and trees are
              covered, its fences and timers kept. Needs a 2MB Next. Off by
              default. Source: Painted cars, circuits and menu: Jon Attree.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing

  Note        The four cars are Next sprites over the game's own cars, which
              still decide every collision. Game logic is unchanged. The base
              keeps the game's own car shapes and colours and fits a 1MB Next.
              Enhanced colours paints the cars, on any Next. Backgrounds adds
              a painted picture for each of the 25 circuits and the menu, and
              needs a 2MB Next. Engines adds an engine note for every car and
              crash and skid noise on the Next's sound chips; the game's own
              beeper sound stays. Known issues: a short pause while a
              circuit's picture is unpacked; Engines does not follow the
              game's SOUND OFF setting; on the Next's own loader Backgrounds
              cannot be chosen together with Enhanced colours or Engines yet.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  One minute qualifying
   2  Easy computer cars
   3  Hard computer cars

  Written for this patch and tested against this exact release: qualifying of
  one minute; computer cars slower or faster through the game's own skill
  setting. All off by default.

